      "problem": "Solve for $k$ where $\\frac{9k-5}{6}=\\frac{k}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9k-5}{6} & =\\frac{k}{2} \\\\ (9k-5)\\cdot 2 & =6\\cdot k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9k-5)\\cdot 2 & =6\\cdot k \\\\ 18k-10 & =6k \\\\ 18k-10-18k & =6k-18k \\\\ -10 & =-12k \\\\ \\frac{-10}{-12} & =\\frac{-12k}{-12} \\\\ \\frac{10}{12} & =k \\\\ \\frac{5}{6} & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $k=\\frac{5}{6}.$",
